reviews": 8, "playtime_forever": 24593, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 354, "playtime_at_review": 23802, "last_played": 1788913958, "avatar": "118d19b306236de4f6956987bc7c8b6ae8294ea2"}, "language": "english", "review": "I love this game, and I’m posting this review in hopes that the developers see it.\n\nI completely understand that major updates take time and may not come frequently, but at this point, it genuinely feels like the game has been abandoned. There’s an entire currency dedicated to Decks and free cosmetics, yet we haven’t seen a new one in five months.\n\nI don’t even play the game that much, and I’ve accumulated enough currency to buy an entire Deck. That feels like a flawed system and, more importantly, a huge missed opportunity to keep players engaged with the game.\n\nIt also feels like most of the focus has shifted toward putting skins in the store instead of offering free Decks and cosmetics. From the outside, that can make it feel like a cash grab, and I really hope that isn’t the case.\n\nI genuinely like this game and want to see it succeed. I’m not asking for constant major updates—just some meaningful use of the systems already in place and a reason for longtime players to stay engaged.", "timestamp_created": 1786143927, "timestamp_updated": 1786143927, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.512658238410949707", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1761816609", "reactions": []}]}